sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant API as FastAPI /upload/har/analyze
    participant Redis
    participant Celery as Celery Worker
    participant Ingestion as Ingestion Service
    participant Normalization as Normalization Service
    participant SchemaInf as Schema Inference
    participant Workflows as Workflow Clustering
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    User->>API: POST /upload/har/analyze (fichier .har)
    API->>API: Valider le fichier + sauvegarder sur disque
    API->>Redis: setex job:{job_id} → status: "queued"
    API-->>User: HTTP 202 Accepted { job_id }

    API->>Celery: process_har_pipeline.apply_async(job_id, file_path, ...)

    Celery->>Redis: setex job:{job_id} → status: "processing"

    Note over Celery,Ingestion: Étape 1 — Ingestion
    Celery->>Ingestion: process_har_file(file_path)
    Ingestion->>Ingestion: parse_har_file() → raw entries
    Ingestion->>Ingestion: clean_traffic() → supprime bruit
    Ingestion->>Ingestion: score_entries() (LLM AI) → filtre candidats API
    Ingestion-->>Celery: cleaned_entries[]

    Note over Celery,Normalization: Étape 2 — Normalisation
    Celery->>Normalization: normalize_entries(cleaned_entries)
    Normalization->>Normalization: normalize_path() → URLs normalisées
    Normalization->>Normalization: build_canonical_key()
    Normalization->>Normalization: deduplicate_endpoints()
    Normalization-->>Celery: normalized_endpoints[]

    Note over Celery,SchemaInf: Étape 3 — Inférence de schéma
    Celery->>SchemaInf: infer_schemas_for_endpoints(normalized_endpoints)
    SchemaInf->>SchemaInf: Analyser request/response bodies
    SchemaInf-->>Celery: schema_results[]

    Note over Celery,Workflows: Étape 4 — Clustering workflows
    Celery->>Workflows: discover_workflows(normalized_endpoints)
    Workflows->>Workflows: Classifier + détecter dépendances
    Workflows-->>Celery: workflows[]

    Note over Celery,DB: Étape 5 — Persistance
    Celery->>DB: save_registry_results(run, endpoints, workflows)
    DB-->>Celery: run_id, saved_endpoints, saved_workflows

    Celery->>Redis: setex job:{job_id} → status: "completed", result: {...}

    User->>API: GET /jobs/{job_id}
    API->>Redis: getex job:{job_id}
    Redis-->>API: { status, result }
    API-->>User: { run_id, normalized_endpoints, saved_workflows, ... }
